<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>
  <!-- The vehicle's Morse key (Radio 0.40.0; docs/development/radio-logbook-qsl-sstv-morse.md, the owner's card of 27 Nov 2026: "In touch,
       and advice at a quarter"): a key and a CW unit for the vehicle's control radio, in the Morse key bay every land vehicle has
       (Loadouts_Default.xml). With a station's key at home, the convoy keeps in touch by Morse where voice cannot reach. It draws nothing worth
       counting. Cost, research, weight, work and skill are agent defaults. It borrows the repeater kit's picture until its own icon is drawn.
       Not yet tested in game. -->
  <Phobos.VehicleSystems.PhobosVehicleFittingDef>
    <defName>PhobosFitting_MorseKey</defName>
    <iconPath>Phobos/Radio/Fittings/RepeaterKit</iconPath>
    <label>Morse key</label>
    <description>A Morse key and a narrow CW unit for the vehicle's control radio. With a base station at home that has a Morse key too, a convoy keeps in touch with home by Morse far beyond the reach of voice: slow, and no speech, but enough to stay in touch and to be talked through by code. It needs the remote control kit's radio.</description>
    <roles><li>MorseKeyMount</li></roles>
    <materials><Steel>6</Steel><ComponentIndustrial>1</ComponentIndustrial></materials>
    <kilograms>2</kilograms>
    <work>600</work>
    <minSkill>2</minSkill>
    <researchPrerequisite>PhobosRadio_LocalRadio</researchPrerequisite>
    <grants><li>RadioMorse</li></grants>
  </Phobos.VehicleSystems.PhobosVehicleFittingDef>
</Defs>
